(different suit from Bamboo) and not honors; they dilute the Half Flush possibility. Among these, **B1** is a terminal but not an honor; B2 and B3 are simples. Half Flush requires only one suit + honors, so keeping Dots hurts that plan. Since B1 is a terminal but not an honor and we have no B1 chow possibility (B1,B2,B3 not consecutive because B4 is depleted), it\u2019s safest to discard first.  \n\nAmong honors: F1 (prevailing wind) and F3 (seat wind) are worth keeping for potential pung points. F2 is not my wind or prevailing, less useful. But currently F2 is only one copy, so also safe to discard later.  \n\nFor Bamboo: T4 pair, T6 triple, T7 pair \u2014 these are good for pungs/chows. T6 triple is already a concealed pung if I keep it; useful for All Pungs.  \n\nSo priority discard: **B1** (Dots, not helping Half Flush, not part of any easy chow).  \n\n**Answer:** Play B1"}
